### RUN .setup for group D (securemode-2026-10-23T1304): AWPTCM-T44287 CryptSecureMode.
### Cut from group C's run .setup; declares ONLY swi_d (u2, the DUT), per STANDING-ORDERS §6.
###
### This session's dispatch gives `consoles: u2 ONLY`. This case needs no partner switch: the
### SAFE HALF that this unattended window runs is entirely read-only on the DUT's own console.
### u3 (swi_b) and u5 (swi_a) are absent from this file entirely -- no [switch], no [baudrates],
### no [power], no [powerlink], no [boot_from_flash], no [portlink] touching them.
###
### 🔴 NO FRAMEWORK RUN IN THIS GROUP, and NO DEVICE-STATE CHANGE AT ALL. The enable limb
###    (`crypto secure-mode`) is BLOCKED for this unattended window by the Test Engineer's own
###    instruction -- see the queue's T44287 triage answer. Nothing here can trigger a power
###    cycle, because nothing here fails a TestCase.
###
### 🔴 swi_d has TWO power supplies, outlets 1 AND 8 on 10.36.230.212. The [power] stanza takes
###    ONE outlet, so a framework-initiated power cycle CANNOT actually cut this unit: the cycle
###    "completes", both PSU bays still read Ok, and only uptime shows nothing happened. A real
###    power cut needs both outlets together (`tools/tb pdu tb277 10.36.230.212 1 cycle` AND
###    `... 8 cycle`). Recorded so a silent no-op is never mistaken for a reboot.
###
### The eth3 <-> port1.0.10 vlan10 L3 underlay and the eth4 <-> port1.0.48 802.1X leg (group A's
### rig, dot1x-controlled with no supplicant authenticated, so eth4 reads CHECK_CABLE) are left
### exactly as group C handed them over. Group D is the last group; this is what /wrap-dt records.
### The box has NO deployed /home/st-art/configs/tb277.setup; never bind one.

[power]
pwr_d = (pdu, 10.36.230.212, 1)

[switch]
swi_d = /dev/u2

[baudrates]
swi_d = 115200

[stack]

[configured_stackport]

[powerlink]
swi_d = pwr_d

[boot_from_flash]
swi_d = True

[portlink]
tb-swi_d = eth3-port1.0.10, eth4-port1.0.48
